From d3528b8e93901ee3a00fef66d91b8ba126c1c3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adhemerval Zanella <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:29:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: Fix stack buffer overflow in loader error messages
 (bug 34541)

Use _dl_exception_create_format instead string operation on a fixed
buffer, which allocates a message of the exact size.

The powerpc32 and powerpc64 _dl_reloc_overflow implementations
are consolidated and the powerpc32 message now says "reloc at" instead
of "relocation at" (as on powerpc64).

The new tst-reloc-overflow and tst-localentry (powerpc64le) tests load a
module that must be rejected because of an out of range R_PPC*_ADDR16
relocation, or because of a PLT call optimized with --plt-localentry
that resolves to a function with a non-zero local entry point.  Both use
a symbol name of more than 8 KiB, and check that dlerror reports it.
tst-localentry-mod is built with -mno-pcrel, since ld does not apply the
localentry optimization to PC-relative calls.

Checked on powerpc-linux-gnu, powerpc64-linux-gnu, and
powerpc64le-linux-gnu (also with --with-cpu=power10).

Co-authored-by: Florian Weimer <fweimer@redhat.com>
Reviewed-by: Peter Bergner <bergner@tenstorrent.com>
(cherry picked from commit cae50527eec1498a9030245036658bee47fc0e04)
